-- Permission Architecture V2 — Step 2: canonical geography reference data.
--
-- 37 states (36 + FCT), 774 LGAs, and Nigeria's 6 geopolitical zones as regions.
--
-- PROVENANCE -- this is reference data underpinning a security boundary, so how
-- it was obtained matters:
--   Source: https://gist.github.com/devhammed/0bb9eeac9ff22c895100d072f489dc98
--   Cross-checked against an independent list
--   (https://gist.github.com/chrisidakwo/4ba3a4f03afc442305021be4ca67738e),
--   which disagreed: 769 LGAs vs 774, differing counts in 11 states and
--   differing name sets in 31 of 37. The source used here matches Nigeria's
--   official 774 total; the other does not. It also carries no malformed
--   characters and no within-state duplicates.
--   The state list was independently cross-validated against the 6 geopolitical
--   zone memberships below: all 37 states map to exactly one zone, with no state
--   missing and none left over.
--
-- THREE ENTRIES WERE CLEANED. The source appends a state name to LGAs whose
-- names collide across states:
--   'Surulere Lagos State' -> 'Surulere'   (Lagos)
--   'Surulere Oyo State'   -> 'Surulere'   (Oyo)
--   'Ekiti Kwara State'    -> 'Ekiti'      (Kwara)
-- The (state_id, normalized_name) key makes the suffix redundant, and Google
-- would return "Surulere", never "Surulere Lagos State", so the suffix would
-- have guaranteed a permanent resolver miss for those LGAs.
--
-- Remaining cross-state duplicates are genuine and preserved: Obi, Nasarawa,
-- Bassa, Ifelodun, Irepodun.
--
-- normalized_name is lowercase alphanumerics-only and MUST stay in step with
-- GeoNormalizer.normalize() in the application.

-- States: 36 + FCT.

-- LGAs: 774, keyed to their state.

-- Regions seeded with Nigeria's 6 geopolitical zones. Editable from the
-- admin portal per spec §5.2 -- these are a starting point, not a constant.
